  "verbalization": "(-)-Rosmarinic Acid appears to interact with Peptide deformylase through a multi-step mechanism, as evidenced by its target relationship with Taste receptor type 2 member 31, which in turn is targeted by Cornuside and Sugiol. These compounds, all of which are linked to (-)-Rosmarinic Acid, ultimately direct their targets to Peptide deformylase. The evidence suggests that (-)-Rosmarinic Acid may modulate the activity of these receptors, which are involved in the degradation of peptides, and that this modulation could lead to a downstream effect on Peptide deformylase. The presence of multiple pathways converging on Peptide deformylase indicates a potential role in metabolic or cellular processes that are influenced by the interaction between (-)-Rosmarinic Acid and its targets. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible dependency on the activity of Peptide deformylase, which may be a key player in the metabolic regulation of these compounds.",
